  "narrative": "This batch delivers decisive robustness evidence for the accepted core dataset associations and several informative negative or inconclusive new probes. For H59, PTEN loss remains associated with much stronger STAT3 dependency under adequate Cas9 activity (signed estimate +0.224, 95% CI +0.159 to +0.289; exposed n=161). The effect is large, excludes null, and is far above the approximate 10% relative threshold for STAT3 dependency (roughly a 0.028 mean-score shift near the overall STAT3 mean), so it is accepted and closed as a QC robustness stratum for H17. H105 strengthens H17 further: in high-EMT cells, PTEN loss is associated with stronger STAT3 dependency (+0.378, CI +0.261 to +0.495; exposed n=58). Although the exposed cell is modest, the interval is tight enough and the effect is well above the approximate threshold; accepted and closed. H106 and H107 similarly confirm the KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 and MSI-high/WRN associations in a high-serum culture context: KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency is enormous (+0.814, CI +0.788 to +0.840), and MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency remains enormous (+0.784, CI +0.746 to +0.823). Both exclude null, are far above clinically meaningful thresholds for those outcomes, and are accepted as robustness strata and closed. H77 confirms that TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency even under adequate Cas9 activity (+0.426, CI +0.339 to +0.513), far above the approximate 0.018 threshold for USP7 dependency; accepted and closed. Because H17 now has strong overall and robustness evidence but lacks independent validation, I request independent validation of H17 rather than H7 or H20, whose effects are already extraordinarily precise. The new KRAS co-mutation interaction H86 is not supportive of the claimed TP53-loss-specific enhancement of KRAS dependency (signed interaction -0.018, CI -0.060 to +0.025). Given the failed and imprecise prior KRAS/STK11 refinements and the interval remaining compatible with only a small positive interaction, this is inconclusive but not worth further follow-up; I mark it unresolved and closed. H109 rejects the claimed adenocarcinoma-specific ERBB2 amplification effect: the interaction is negative (-0.051, CI -0.117 to +0.015), and the upper bound is below the approximate 0.026 clinically meaningful threshold for ERBB2 dependency, so a scientifically meaningful adenocarcinoma-enhanced ERBB2 dependency is not supported. H112 rejects TP53 loss associated with stronger DHX9 dependency: the signed estimate is negative (-0.020, CI -0.039 to -0.001), indicating the opposite direction, though not a strongly meaningful reversed effect worth promoting now. H113 rejects KRAS mutation associated with weaker BRAF dependency (+0? signed -0.016, CI -0.034 to +0.001; claimed positive/upper below threshold). H111, H114, and H115 remain unresolved and deferred: each point estimate is below or near the approximate clinical threshold and the intervals are too broad or include null; further follow-up is possible but should not crowd out more robust core claims. All statements remain observational associations within this supplied dataset, not causal mechanisms or claims of external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Current core accepted dataset associations: H5 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency (accepted, validated); H7 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency (accepted, robust, not independently validated); H17 PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency (accepted, robust, independent validation requested now); H20 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency (accepted, robust, not independently validated); H73 TP53 loss -> weaker USP7 dependency (accepted, validated). This batch accepted and closed robustness strata H59 STAT3/Cas9-QC, H105 STAT3/high-EMT, H106 NFE2L2/high-serum, H107 WRN/high-serum, H77 USP7/Cas9-QC. New negative/inconclusive probes: H109 ERBB2/adenocarcinoma interaction rejected; H112 TP53/stronger DHX9 rejected in claimed direction; H113 KRAS/weaker BRAF rejected; H86 KRAS interaction with TP53 loss unresolved but closed; H111 MYC/KIF18A, H114 TP53/MDM2 in high MYC expression, and H115 EGFR amplification in KRAS-wildtype adenocarcinoma remain unresolved and deferred. Validation request set to H17 because it is a central accepted association with moderate effect and strong but non-independent evidence. Avoid promoting KRAS co-mutation subgroup claims after H48 and H96 validation failures. Next priorities: assess H17 validation when it arrives, preserve validated core conclusions, and only spend remaining analyses on highly informative robustness or biologically plausible unresolved RTK/DNA-repair effects."
